URL:https://tockify.com/distilleryevents/detail/707/1786593600000
SUMMARY: Revolutionary Women in Blues
DESCRIPTION:The Blues is the sound of cultural resilience\, and while the
  genre is the foundation for modern music\, the stories of the women who 
 shaped it are often unseen and unheard.\n\nSister Rosetta Tharpe\, Ma Rai
 ney\, and Bessie Smith lived exciting\, courageous\, and wild lives\, all
  while quietly shaping American culture through music and more. Ma Rainey
  is now known as The Mother of Blues\, Sister Rosetta as The Godmother of
  Rock & Roll\, and Bessie Smith as\, The Empress Of Blues.\n\nJoin creato
 r and star Divine Brown (Billie\, Sarah and Ella: Revolutionary Women in 
 Jazz) and an all-star team of performers and musicians as they bring us t
 he story of these three extraordinary and revolutionary women.\n\nWORLD P
 REMIERE
CATEGORIES:
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/575f0c12df82fe
 6ce68f57cb/6a4c64a5892b27f8db0df643/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:The Blues is the sound of cultural resilience\, and 
 while the genre is the foundation for modern music\, the stories of the w
 omen who shaped it are often...
